    "annotations_dropped": [
      {
        "annotation_id": "7e0a91f6fb4e4bddb690f27dc2378029_34",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "RLC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The trial Court, on an analysis of the oral and documentary evidence, granted divorce, dissolving the marriage between the appellant and the respondent, against which, the respondent/wife preferred appeal, which was allowed, setting aside t"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "376c50b9a0954158a4536bd8616b0c14_40",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "RLC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Though the divorce petition filed by the husband was allowed only on the ground of cruelty, however, the learned trial Judge found that the appellant/husband has not proved the ground of adultery."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0582ea0130bc4140b459b9f612ceea5a_41",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "RLC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_labels:RLC"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The respondent/wife challenged the order of divorce passed by the trial Court by filing appeal before the District Court in C.M.A.No.36 of 2012, which was heard by the appellate Court and allowed, by setting aside the order passed by the tr"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f76c49f189514efd90fb19fafdbd3ce9_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "A consideration of the cases cited on behalf of the appellant therefore shows that most of them are not exactly in point so far as the facts of the present case are concerned."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "18fed119d9ac485d95e022bbdeb35ea7_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Our conclusion on the question of res judicata raised in the present appeals is this."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1a4a158ed3c64d31a61f7e5d4a3fbf15_49",
        "summary_section": "issue",
        "labels": [
          "ISSUE"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:issue"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Where the trial Court has decided two suits having common issues on Sivabalan vs Maheswari on 19 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/159931443/\n3 the merits and there are two appeals there-from and one of them is dismiss"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "019f918348b74b72bdebe8efced52762_50",
        "summary_section": "issue",
        "labels": [
          "ISSUE"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:issue"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In such a case the result of the decision of the appeal Court is to confirm the decision of the trial Court given on merits, and if that is so the decision of the appeal court will be res judicata whatever may be the reason for the dismissa"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "694453b0fb204def8db49bf9c91f3b25_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nTherefore, mere non-filing of any appeal against the dismissal of the counter- claim, will not operate as res-judicata."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c38b8c4c0a6242978ef01d6870461bd2_53",
        "summary_section": "issue",
        "labels": [
          "ISSUE"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:issue"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The issue involved is as to whether the appellant is entitled for divorce on the ground of adultery and also cruelty."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bf56bb438f02467cac0ce89f6eb48ef6_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As far as the adultery is concerned, the trial Court dis-allowed it and there was no further appeal."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "cf4a6bfe488a46a08a058c1474b1df4b_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As far as the cruelty is concerned, the trial Court failed to appreciate the evidence and the trial Court also misconceived the evidence of R.W.2 and granted divorce as if the respondent-wife caused mental cruelty."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c6e7f5733368490094d4f5f6cefdef2c_56",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
            "matched_text": "set aside",
            "start": 103,
            "end": 112
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "But the appellate Court being the final Court of fact-finding, rightly re-appreciated the evidence and set aside the order passed by the trial Court."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "70f0197aeed54256b432ddeaa26ee994_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As far as the first substantial question of law is concerned, the appellant/husband has stated that the wife went for delivery and later on, she did not turn up and without any valid reason, she had left the matrimonial home https://www.mhc"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "764967fb72f249af9596d52c9fa76886_59",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, the trial Court rightly dis-allowed the petition for restitution of conjugal rights and that the appellant has also not challenged the same."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "87524972283741e5a498a94c37fb1743_60",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n13. As far as the cruelty is concerned, the appellant-husband has pleaded that the respondent mixed poison in the food and had threatened/black-mailed him that she would give false complaint against him, which caused him cruelty."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1291e45c54ce4634998663605827ab80_61",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Though the respondent has stated that there is no problem with the appellant and only the mother is the cause for their separation and the appellant/husband was only examined as a witness, but the appellant has not examined his mother and h"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "723742c7410f4dc580bb15b8beee7975_62",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The appellant has also not stated that only the wife had mixed the poison in the presence of anybody."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5f8c0ba51bfa4d44b06150ca48e0529b_63",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Only he suspected her and R.W.2 stated that https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis only the mother of the appellant alone informed that the respondent/wife mixed poison in the food."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0f6a1ed9e3c14984bf4e5276c247c9a5_64",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Based on that, the appellant has asked about the same from the respondent and she denied the same."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d5a7afa481b04435bbd0d2d479c98029_65",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Further, in this case, the food also was not sent for Forensic Laboratory for analysis and there was no eye-witness to the incident relating to mixing of poison."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7679a4e28a524fdd8b26cd06c2dc0e51_66",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Already the respondent made allegation against her mother-in-law (ie. the mother of the appellant) who was playing tricks between the appellant and the respondent, but the appellant has not examined his mother and no eye-witness was examine"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4ffdde4fd0e4433eb7bb7476be33b6d5_67",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Moreover, the said suspected food also was not sent for Forensic Department for analysis to find out that as to whether there was any poison in the suspected food that would be served on the appellant and also that no Police complaint was g"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2dd2f9258f3243a882646ef2c48a7b23_68",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, the trial Court failed to appreciate the evidence in the absence of any materials and found that the respondent had caused mental cruelty to the appellant-husband, whereas, the first appellate Court rightly re-appreciated the evi"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a09c8529b97640398e10919fe1d7d7f1_69",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The appellant has not also proved that the respondent-wife https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis threatened/black-mailed that she would give false complaint."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "367d3908289740768c7fa8c496fd8c3c_70",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The appellant though suspected the character of the respondent-wife, and he pleaded adultery, but admittedly, out of their wed-lock, one child was born and the appellant has not given any DNA test for denying the paternity of the child."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "17399c0126cb4301b20baa2efc5b03c5_71",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "14. Therefore, in the above circumstances, when the ground of adultery was also dis-allowed, the appellant-husband has not filed any appeal or cross appeal/objection."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a8d79938920740a5b745151208d905f3_72",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, this Court finds that the respondent has left the matrimonial home only due to the reason that she was conceived and she went to the paternal home only for delivery of the baby and not for any other purpose."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1dc35c60ee6a4d9f9713e1c5677bad83_73",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Later on,\nthere was misunderstanding between them and it is not the evidence of the appellant that he persuaded her to come back and she refused to come."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b55e2f152a984f5eab850bdd48b74ae7_74",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "No independent witness was examined and even the mother of the appellant has not stated that they have taken effective steps to bring her back to matrimonial home."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4704a5ad74224446a875a2d19ee4db69_75",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The main allegation of the respondent is that even the appellant suspected her character and either the appellant or his mother came to her parental home even for seeing the child."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a85bf307e7ed42c48bd16f81a225d919_76",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "As the appellant has not examined any independent witness either for the allegation of mixing of poison in the food and also with regard to the threat/black-mail of giving a false complaint and she left the matrimonial home without any vali"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ef5969c1bd514105a99ab5d89cf0c373_77",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The respondent/wife examined herself as R.W.1 and denied all the allegations made https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis by the appellant and she also examined R.Ws.2 and 3."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b88be9473e8f405a81c0e798d107fbdd_78",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "R.W.3 is the father and though he has deposed in his chief examination that he has only supported the case of the respondent, during cross-examination, the appellant has put a suggestion that he asked about the mixing of poison and the moth"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1e08729542c94545bcbf21da6e2198c7_79",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "R.W.2 admittedly stated that the appellant suspected her and there was some misunderstanding and the husband suspected the fidelity of the wife and adultery allegation was not proved and the appellant has not challenged that finding and eve"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "cea1f9165c1d436abcc744aab9993c6c_80",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "5 trial Court failed to appreciate the evidence in right perspective and the first appellate Court re- appreciated the evidence and allowed the appeal, though the appellant has not proved that the respondent/wife left the matrimonial home w"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6eab20c6b4fd41189a82d39124d3a300_81",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The first substantial question of law is answered accordingly against the appellant/husband."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1506748ebc744dcbaaf4f80d2ebbe3cf_82",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "15. As far as the second substantial question of law is concerned, though the appellant filed the petition for divorce, counter-claim was filed by the wife and she also filed a petition for restitution of conjugal rights, the counter-claim "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f1597c6a36df4f12b29fd0aecf9dc1f0_83",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The allegations are vice-versa."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "10aeca49edc14ed08b83352146156da9_84",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis the above circumstances, the trial Court granted divorce only on the ground of mental cruelty and not on the ground of adultery."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a28da858ad7e442b95b5b7b5bb5275dd_85",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The appellant did not challenge the findings of adultery."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "674429e54eeb4f9ab0ecd0073fc776f1_86",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However, the respondent-wife challenged the findings of cruelty and the appellate Court allowed the appeal."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c62cbb1b39c74cb1b30b84e98cd04457_87",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Mere non-filing of the appeal against the dismissal of the counter-claim may not operate as res- judicata."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "33c882ba85e243a2b9a53e64c30df815_88",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
